# Shazdown Mmw (bouyonmusique.com, wave 26 parity, 2026-10-20)
# Sources used (all opened 2026-10-20):
# - Bandcamp, Soundway Records, Road Fever album page: compilation released May 9, 2025, compiled by Rozaly, mastering and vinyl cut The Carvery, vinyl pressing Garcia & Co, design Wolfe Hall Studio, photography Selwyn De Wind; vinyl Side A track 3 Shazdown Mmw, Bouyon Beam Riddim, 3:20; digital listing track 3 Shazdown, Bouyon Beam (2015), track 20 Shazdown, Bouyon Truth Riddim (Digital Only) (2023), 3:43, track 21 Shazdown, Bouyon 3004 Riddim (Digital Only) (2022), 2:21; notes describe instrumental Dennery Segment and Bouyon riddims originally made for vocalists, minimal 150+ BPM, FL percussion packs, DJ and vox samples and synth riffs, bridging trap, drill, dancehall, sped up Haitian konpa and Angolan kuduro, and state in one sentence that Dominica increasingly influential Bouyon sound thrives through ScarnX and Guadeloupe-based Shazdown Mmw & DJ Demafidem; cassette is a 55 and a half minute mix by DJ Intl Prostyle with the full 26 track digital download, while the digital listing shown on the page counts 25 tracks.
# - Shazam, Bouyon Truth Riddim song page (opened): released May 9, 2025 by Soundway Records Ltd as part of the album Road Fever EP1, BPM 159; credits list Shazdown Mmw as Performer, Abel Fontange for Drum Programming and as Composer, and Frank Merritt as Mastering Engineer. This profile reports those credits as track credits only; no opened source states that Abel Fontange is the person behind the Shazdown Mmw name, so no identity claim is printed.
# - Resident Advisor, Road Fever review by Cameron Cook, published May 21, 2025: 25 track list with the three Shazdown tracks at positions 3, 20 and 21; the review gives the only critic descriptions of the two digital only tracks (Bouyon Truth Riddim: ear-needling synths and bleating horns ricocheting like a pinball machine, an unsettling underground dance floor quality; Bouyon 3004 Riddim: an erupting keyboard motif that roars like a semi truck), and places Shazdown on the Dominica side, which contradicts the label notes that say Guadeloupe-based; this profile follows the label notes and flags the gap.
# - Bandcamp Daily, Album of the Day review by Maria Barrios, May 12, 2025: London based Soundway Records, carnival riddims, Dennery segment and bouyon at 140 BPM or faster, laptop and Fruity Loops production; it names On Di Road and Bouyon Beam together, with punchy intros featuring synth stabs and vocal samples, as examples of the producers reimagining traditional music through laptop production. No Shazdown biography.
# - Patta, Road Fever feature (published May 12, 2025): compiled by Amsterdam based, Curacao raised Rozaly, mixed by DJ Intl Prostyle in Saint Lucia, 55 and a half minutes, BPM rarely dips below 150, Shazdown Mmw listed among the contributing production crews, the compilation zeroes in on Dennery Segment from Saint Lucia and Bouyon from Dominica and Guadeloupe, out on vinyl, digital and limited cassette, with a short film by Rozaly and Selwyn De Wind.
# Searches with no result (2026-10-20): no standalone Shazdown Mmw artist page, biography, interview, real name explanation of the Mmw suffix, or solo release outside Road Fever was found on Spotify, Apple Music, Deezer, Qobuz, SoundCloud, Audiomack, YouTube or Discogs during this research. This profile prints none of those things and carries exactly three recordings in its structured data, all from the opened label page.

